# Monorepo environment variables — keep the surface small

## Pyramid Layer

- Layer: L1 operational rule.

## Use This When

- Start here whenever a task proposes a new env var, alias, or shared runtime setting.

## Stop Here If

- Stop once it is clear whether a new env name is justified.

## Descend To

- Continue within this file for naming and reuse guidance.

## When to add a new `process.env` / compose key

- Add a **new** variable name only when **two or more** runtime or deployment pieces must read the **same** value (server + worker, CI + app, etc.), **or** you already have (or plan) a **single** operator/settings layer that injects it.
- **Do not** introduce parallel aliases for the same concept in one process unless each name is **actually** read by a different shared integration and cannot be unified.

## Prefer reuse

- Reuse **existing** monorepo names (`SUPABASE_URL`, `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`, `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`, `PORT`, …) so `.env` stays copy-paste aligned across apps.
- Fixed infrastructure contracts (queue/stream names, durable consumer names, subject prefixes) belong in **code** (a shared package, local `const`) — not in env — unless multiple repos or operators must diverge without redeploying code.

## Agent checklist

1. Before adding `FOO_SERVICE_URL`, check whether **`BAR` already used elsewhere** can carry the same value.
2. Before env-toggling a constant, ask: will **another** service read this same key? If no, prefer a **typed constant** in the package.
